<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shan State</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shan State is the largest state of Myanmar, covering the Shan Plateau in the east of the country. It was formed in 1948 from the Federated Shan States when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> became independent, after Shan leaders agreed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panglong-conference">Panglong Conference</a> of 1947 to join the new Union. In 1959 the hereditary saophas gave up their ruling powers to the Shan State government, ending the old principalities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shan-state.jpg" alt="Shan State" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stefan Fussan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pindaya_Caves_0001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
